## Layout

```
design/          the as-designed record -- Claude Design's output
  brief.md       the order a drop answers
  RETURN.md      the drop's narrative
  index.md       what is present, and in what state
  kit/           the neutral kit every artefact imports
  assets/<slug>/ one directory per asset, flat
  notes/         durable thinking that is not an asset
  site/          generated microsite over the above
cdsync.json       this venture's facts, in one place
```

Everything outside `design/` is the as-built record. The two are kept apart
deliberately -- see `AGENTS.md`.

## Getting a design drop

```sh
# 1. fill in cdsync.json -- especially `fixed`, `open`, and `order`
# 2. assemble the brief
cdsync brief

# 3. give design/brief.md to Claude Design, let it work, export a zip
# 4. unpack it
cdsync import ~/Downloads/drop.zip

# 5. hold it against its own specs
cdsync check

# 6. read it
cdsync site
```

`cdsync brief` inlines every ordered asset's full specification, so the brief is
complete on its own. Nothing in it points at a file the reader cannot open.
